# Milestone: M3
# Covers: ambient tag chain is inherited by strands spawned via the `,`
#         (fork-detach) separator; tag.stop() on the ambient tag cascades to
#         the parallel strand (row 11 §4.3 + T38 separator runtime).
#
# blocked: compile error — `,` fork-detach separator inside tag-scope body not supported
# matrix-row: tag-ambient
#
# Reason (updated v0.13.5 probe):
#   v0.13.5 fixed `&`/`|` block operands in the PARSER.  That fix is
#   irrelevant here: the blocker is the EMITTER refusing `,` inside a
#   `t: { ... }` tag-scope body with a compile error.  OP_FORK_DETACH guard
#   was removed by LANG-S06; the remaining gap is that the emitter's
#   fork-detach emit path does not track the tag-scope nesting context, so
#   `t: { expr , expr }` fails to compile.  Unchanged since v0.13.4.
#
# Urbiscript source (re-activate when , inside tag-scope emitter path works):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   var log = "";
#   t: { log = log + "outer", { log = log + "inner" | t.stop() } };
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "outer"
